Button groups without a card behind them: the page's Save bar and the dialogs' footers

Two places drew a surface of their own behind a row of buttons that already have their own:

- Every form page ends in Reset / Save / Save & Apply, docked to the bottom right of the view
  inside a frosted card: a second border, a blurred background and a large shadow. On most
  pages that card is the only thing at the bottom of the view, so it read as a stray box
  rather than as part of the page.
- Every dialog (the changes list, the upload dialog, section editors, confirmations) put its
  buttons on a shaded footer strip with a rule above it, bled out to the dialog's edges.

Both are gone. The Save bar keeps no background, border, blur, padding or shadow; it stays
sticky, so the buttons still float at the bottom right while the page scrolls, and each button
carries a soft shadow of its own so it stays legible over the content under it. A dialog's
buttons sit on the dialog itself, right-aligned below its content, with no strip and no button
shadows.

Applies to: https://github.com/anothaDev/luci-theme-vantage.git @ v1.2.0 (a7ff63b7), after 0001 and 0002.
Upstream status: local to CleanWRT.

